      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 52-year-old woman presented with recurrent urinary tract infections and flank pain. Both an abdominal CT-scan and a plain abdominal X-ray showed bilateral nephrocalcinosis and a kidney stone in the left ureter. These findings are suggestive of medullary sponge kidneys."},
